            <ArticleTitle>An Unusual Cause of Hemopericardium 22 Years After a Fontan Procedure.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e187-e189</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0003-4975(16)30879-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.athoracsur.2016.06.108</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Late tamponade after cardiac operations is rare but reasonably well described. We report a case of exceedingly late tamponade secondary to a spontaneous coronary bleed 22 years after a Fontan operation, which was repaired with catheter intervention.</AbstractText>
